      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It's not settled. In carefully planned short-term studies where vegan and omnivorous diets supplied the same calories and protein, older adults showed no significant difference in muscle protein synthesis. In real-world trials where people chose their own meals, plant-based eaters tended to eat less protein — and that, along with calories, is hard to separate from the protein source itself. The practical answer: plant protein can work, but you need to plan for enough of it."
